{"vid":"LiRDPpNE4rs","source":"LiRDPpNE4rs.en-en.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":3.3,"txt":"You're learning with 925 English - Business English for the workplace."},{"t":14.6,"txt":"Hi Tim here with another nine to five english lesson."},{"t":20.9,"txt":"Today we're going to learn how to give instructions in english."},{"t":27.7,"txt":"Telling people what to do isn't just something the boss does."},{"t":33,"txt":"Anytime you're helping someone with a problem"},{"t":36.5,"txt":"training someone giving technical advice or telling a colleague how to do"},{"t":43,"txt":"something you're giving instructions."},{"t":47.5,"txt":"Of course it's very important to be clear when you're giving instructions."},{"t":54,"txt":"And for that reason we sometimes explain things"},{"t":58.1,"txt":"step by step in a sequence of instructions. This means"},{"t":64.6,"txt":"using words like first secondly and thirdly."},{"t":71.8,"txt":"Or you might use other words like next and at the end of your sequence"},{"t":80.3,"txt":"finally or lastly. Let's practice some ways of using these"},{"t":87.4,"txt":"words to give a sequence of instruction."},{"t":91.4,"txt":"Listen to each example then repeat it for yourself"},{"t":96.5,"txt":"Ready let's get started."},{"t":100.7,"txt":"First try closing the program and opening it again."},{"t":110.7,"txt":"Secondly i'd like you to complete the rest of the form."},{"t":120.6,"txt":"Next you'll have to choose a password."},{"t":129.7,"txt":"Finally don't forget to log out at the end of the session."},{"t":140.8,"txt":"So did those instructions sound like orders i mean do you think"},{"t":147.8,"txt":"giving instructions means saying do this and do that well"},{"t":155.8,"txt":"not exactly in fact in english we don't like to be too direct"},{"t":162,"txt":"in most situations that's why we say"},{"t":166.7,"txt":"can you try closing the program instead of"},{"t":170.1,"txt":"close the program or you'll have to choose a password instead"},{"t":176.2,"txt":"of just choose a password one way to avoid being"},{"t":181.8,"txt":"too direct in english is to use special words"},{"t":186.2,"txt":"called modals modals are words such as can and need to"},{"t":194.6,"txt":"and could and should using modals is easy you just"},{"t":202.7,"txt":"put the modal between you and the main verb for example"},{"t":209.4,"txt":"you might say first you need to open an account"},{"t":217,"txt":"let's try some examples of giving instructions"},{"t":220.8,"txt":"using modals. Remember to repeat the examples after you hear them."},{"t":229.4,"txt":"You'll need to enter your username and password to begin."},{"t":240.3,"txt":"Okay you can now open the app and create an account."},{"t":250.4,"txt":"Could you try restarting your device?"},{"t":259.4,"txt":"You need to start by launching the program from the main menu."},{"t":269.8,"txt":"Did you notice that one example came in the form of a question? that's an"},{"t":276.3,"txt":"extra polite way of telling someone to do something."},{"t":280.9,"txt":"Not every modal can be used that way however. Only can and"},{"t":287.4,"txt":"could will work. For example, could you check if your password is"},{"t":293.8,"txt":"correct is just a nice way of saying check your"},{"t":298.6,"txt":"password is correct you can also combine sequences"},{"t":304.3,"txt":"and modals to find the right balance between being clear"},{"t":309,"txt":"and polite. But what if you're not sure whether you've been clear enough?"},{"t":316.2,"txt":"What if you don't really know whether the other person has understood?"},{"t":322.1,"txt":"fortunately we have lots of different ways of"},{"t":325.4,"txt":"checking understanding. And the best way is just to ask directly like"},{"t":332.1,"txt":"do you understand you might also ask if people are clear or whether"},{"t":339.3,"txt":"everything makes sense these are just different ways of asking if"},{"t":345.1,"txt":"something has been understood let's try some practice with checking"},{"t":350.9,"txt":"understanding using these expressions. Once again"},{"t":355.9,"txt":"repeat the examples after you hear them."},{"t":361.7,"txt":"So is everyone clear on what they have to do?"},{"t":370.4,"txt":"Okay do you understand how this works now?"},{"t":380,"txt":"Does that make sense to you?"},{"t":387.4,"txt":"Any questions about what you need to do?"},{"t":396,"txt":"As you heard one other way to check understanding is to ask if there are any"},{"t":402.3,"txt":"questions. that way you can find out exactly what"},{"t":406.8,"txt":"people don't understand."},{"t":410.3,"txt":"Okay, so we've practiced some useful ways of giving instructions"},{"t":416.2,"txt":"and checking understanding. But what do these expressions"},{"t":420.8,"txt":"sound like in a conversation? Let's listen to a short dialogue between"},{"t":427.8,"txt":"Sean and Kim. Sean has asked for help using a machine"},{"t":434.1,"txt":"and Kim is giving him instructions on how to use it. Let's listen."},{"t":442.7,"txt":"Could you help me with this?"},{"t":445.3,"txt":"Sure, first try turning the machine on."},{"t":449.8,"txt":"Okay i did that what's next?"},{"t":454.3,"txt":"Next you can turn the dial on the front to 50."},{"t":460.1,"txt":"Does that make sense? Kim begins by instructing him to turn the machine on"},{"t":467.8,"txt":"then to turn the dial to 50. She uses the sequence word next"},{"t":474.8,"txt":"and the modal can. Now it's your turn to practice."},{"t":481.3,"txt":"We'll repeat the dialogue but this time we're going to beep out the second"},{"t":487,"txt":"speaker's words. You will have to say those parts"},{"t":491.3,"txt":"yourself. Remember to say that first Sean"},{"t":496.2,"txt":"should turn the machine on then say next and instruct"},{"t":502.8,"txt":"him to turn the dial on the front to 50."},{"t":509.1,"txt":"Could you help me with this?"},{"t":518,"txt":"Okay i did that what's next?"},{"t":530.2,"txt":"All right that's all for this lesson. We've learned some great ways to give"},{"t":536.8,"txt":"instructions and to check understanding."},{"t":541.4,"txt":"We'll be back soon with some more useful english expressions. Until then"},{"t":547.9,"txt":"so long and happy learning!"}],"words":[{"t":3.28,"w":"You're"},{"t":3.28,"w":"learning"},{"t":3.28,"w":"with"},{"t":3.28,"w":"925"},{"t":3.28,"w":"English"},{"t":3.28,"w":"-"},{"t":3.28,"w":"Business"},{"t":3.28,"w":"English"},{"t":3.28,"w":"for"},{"t":3.28,"w":"the"},{"t":3.28,"w":"workplace."},{"t":14.56,"w":"Hi"},{"t":14.56,"w":"Tim"},{"t":14.56,"w":"here"},{"t":14.56,"w":"with"},{"t":14.56,"w":"another"},{"t":14.56,"w":"nine"},{"t":14.56,"w":"to"},{"t":14.56,"w":"five"},{"t":14.56,"w":"english"},{"t":14.56,"w":"lesson."},{"t":20.88,"w":"Today"},{"t":20.88,"w":"we're"},{"t":20.88,"w":"going"},{"t":20.88,"w":"to"},{"t":20.88,"w":"learn"},{"t":20.88,"w":"how"},{"t":20.88,"w":"to"},{"t":20.88,"w":"give"},{"t":20.88,"w":"instructions"},{"t":20.88,"w":"in"},{"t":20.88,"w":"english."},{"t":27.68,"w":"Telling"},{"t":27.68,"w":"people"},{"t":27.68,"w":"what"},{"t":27.68,"w":"to"},{"t":27.68,"w":"do"},{"t":27.68,"w":"isn't"},{"t":27.68,"w":"just"},{"t":27.68,"w":"something"},{"t":27.68,"w":"the"},{"t":27.68,"w":"boss"},{"t":27.68,"w":"does."},{"t":32.96,"w":"Anytime"},{"t":32.96,"w":"you're"},{"t":32.96,"w":"helping"},{"t":32.96,"w":"someone"},{"t":32.96,"w":"with"},{"t":32.96,"w":"a"},{"t":32.96,"w":"problem"},{"t":36.48,"w":"training"},{"t":36.48,"w":"someone"},{"t":36.48,"w":"giving"},{"t":36.48,"w":"technical"},{"t":36.48,"w":"advice"},{"t":36.48,"w":"or"},{"t":36.48,"w":"telling"},{"t":36.48,"w":"a"},{"t":36.48,"w":"colleague"},{"t":36.48,"w":"how"},{"t":36.48,"w":"to"},{"t":36.48,"w":"do"},{"t":43.04,"w":"something"},{"t":43.04,"w":"you're"},{"t":43.04,"w":"giving"},{"t":43.04,"w":"instructions."},{"t":47.52,"w":"Of"},{"t":47.52,"w":"course"},{"t":47.52,"w":"it's"},{"t":47.52,"w":"very"},{"t":47.52,"w":"important"},{"t":47.52,"w":"to"},{"t":47.52,"w":"be"},{"t":47.52,"w":"clear"}